        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Kolkata</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1690 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">The recorded history of the city began in 1690 with the arrival of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">English East India Company</a>. Job Charnock is often regarded as the founder, but in 2003 the Calcutta High Court ruled that the city has no founder.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On the eastern bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hooghly-river">Hooghly River</a> in the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a> Delta, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-bengal">West Bengal</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, about 80 km west of the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bangladesh">Bangladesh</a>.</span></div>
